course: dictionary
lesson: 14209
title: Muffled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Muffled describes a sound that is quiet and unclear because something is in the way. «We could hear muffled voices through the thick door.» The door is between you and the people, so their words are hard to hear. Muffled means quiet and unclear here.
explain: Muffled can also mean a sound that has been made quieter by covering it. «She put a cushion over the alarm clock, so the ringing was muffled.» The cushion covers the sound and makes it softer. Ask yourself: is something covering or blocking the sound?
explain: Muffled up means wrapped up warmly. «Ravi was muffled up in a scarf and hat on the frosty morning.» This is about clothes, not sound. The clues are scarf, hat and frosty, which all point to keeping warm.
fact: Muffled is the past tense of muffle: muffle, muffles, muffled, muffling.
fact: «Muffled» can describe a sound that is quiet and unclear.
fact: «Muffled up» means wrapped up warmly, as in «muffled up in scarves».
fact: Soft things such as cushions, carpets and thick curtains make sounds more muffled, because they soak up sound.
fact: A good check is to swap in quiet and blurry, or wrapped up warmly, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The muffled cry came from behind the wall.» What does muffled mean here? | Happy and excited | Loud and clear | *Quiet and unclear, as if something is in the way | Very bright
exercise: Which word is the past tense of muffle? | muffles | mumbled | *muffled | muffling
exercise: The bell was covered with a cloth, so its ring was ___. Which word fits best? | sharp | *muffled | bright | empty
test: «Footsteps sounded muffled on the thick carpet.» Why do the footsteps sound muffled? | *The thick carpet softens the sound, so it is quieter | The shiny floor made them echo loudly | The footsteps were very fast | The room was full of people shouting
test: Which sentence uses muffled to mean wrapped up warmly? | The muffled voices came from upstairs. | The muffled cry startled the class. | *Tara was muffled up in a big coat and scarf. | The music was muffled by the thick walls.
exam: What does «muffled up» mean? | Hiding in a dark room | Falling over in the snow | Shouting loudly | *Wrapped up warmly
